 "description": "Westerhoff2020 - systems biology model of the coronavirus pandemic 2020\nBioModels BIOMD0000000988 (curated). SBML file: Westerhoff2020.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 365 time units (SED-ML: Westerhoff2020.sedml), sampling 0.35714285714285715.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): MISMATCH_PARTIAL, max |difference| = 1.00e+00 of species peak (worst: infected_nontested_0)\nIndependent check of this deck (SciPy integration with Kintecus semantics) against the SBML: max |difference| = 1.00e+00 of species peak.\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] species 'total_population_0' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] species 'registered_corona_0' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] species 'dead_corona_perc_0' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] species 'recovered_corona_perc_0' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] species 'dead_noncorona_perc_0' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] species 'frac_coronaDeadOfAllDead_0' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] species 'epidemic_extinguished_bool_0' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] species 'infected_tested_div10' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] re1: USER expression is 4495 characters; Kintecus V2027 mis-evaluates USER expressions longer than about 840 characters (see KINTECUS_ISSUES)\n  [blocker] reaction 're1' not converted (rate term is 4495 characters (> 2153))\n  [info] re3: USER expression is 4495 characters; Kintecus V2027 mis-evaluates USER expressions longer than about 840 characters (see KINTECUS_ISSUES)\n  [blocker] reaction 're3' not converted (rate term is 4495 characters (> 2153))\n  [info] 4 species/parameters given short names (Q1...) so USER expressions fit Kintecus's expression length limit; original ids are in the SPECIES comments column\nRenamed species (Kintecus name = SBML id): Q1 = infected_nontested_0; Q2 = infected_tested_0; Q4 = symptoms_tested_0; Q3 = symptoms_nontested_0",
